.TH TELNET 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
telnet \- clients et serveur reseau / network clients and server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B telnet
host [port]
.br
.B ftp
[-n] host [port]
.br
.B httpd
[-p port] [-d root] [-f]
.br
.B traceroute
[-m hops] [-w sec] host
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
telnet negotiates the IAC options (remote ECHO switches the local terminal echo off, SGA is accepted, others refused). ftp is an interactive passive-mode
client: open user ls dir cd cdup pwd get put mkdir rmdir delete rename binary ascii lcd ! quote system size close quit; -n disables the automatic login. httpd
serves static files over HTTP/1.0 (GET, HEAD, index.html, directory listings, 403 for .. paths) from /var/www or -d root. traceroute sends UDP probes with
increasing TTL and reads ICMP replies on a raw socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
nc(1), wget(1), ping(1)
